{"availability":"available","full":"jaccomoc/jactl","name":"jactl","description":"A secure, embeddable, scripting language for Java-based applications.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Java","stars":113,"forks":4,"created":"2022-07-13T21:33:06Z","updated":"2026-10-15T06:29:56Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["apache-license-2","compiler","java","jvm","jvm-bytecode","open-source","programming-language","scripting-language"],"demo":"https://jactl.io/playground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:38.611Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:38.611Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:38.611Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:15.025Z","stars":113,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:19.877Z","stars":113,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:32.074Z","stars":113,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-11T06:13:47.060Z","stars":113,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:59:38.611Z","stars":113,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Jactl is a powerful scripting language for the JVM platform whose syntax is a combination of bits from Java, Groovy, and Perl. It can be run from a REPL and from the commandline for commandline scripts but its main goal is to be integrated into Java applications and provide a secure, locked-down mechanism that customers/users can use to customise the application behaviour.","It is especially suited to event-loop/reactive applications due to its built-in suspend/resume mechanism based on continuations that ensures it never blocks the execution thread on which it is running.",":star: Please consider giving this project a star as a way to encourage me to continue making improvements to Jactl."],"features":["Jactl scripts compile to bytecode to take advantage of the performance capabilities of the JVM."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jaccomoc/jactl/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b94c95d1a5c72f17b3dd7d6a54afb07e0044e1b1f6426d1548979c3ed5bbdfbd","ext